## Key implementation notes

| Component | Critical details honoured |
|---|---|
| **AA battery** | Exact jacket split `−2.4…+1.0` (black, 3.4) / `+1.0…+2.4` (blue, 1.4); lathe-cap with a real **recessed circular groove** (`0.446→0.486` radius valley) and a **0.25-tall nickel nub**; `+` decals are curved cylinder patches (`polygonOffset` prevents z-fighting); total height ≈ 5.24 (body 4.8 + button 0.44). |
| **E10 bulb** | Threads are a **sine-rippled lathe** (5 turns, ±0.032) — one draw call, no torus stacking; teardrop globe lathe with `transmission 0.96 / ior 1.5 / clearcoat 1`; helix filament + posts inside; `setLit()` toggles `emissiveIntensity`, `PointLight` and the additive glow blob together. Glass needs `scene.environment` (PMREM) to look physical. |
| **Mabuchi 130** | `RoundedBoxGeometry(1.5, 1.1, 2.0, 4, 0.26)` gives the flat-sided oval can; boss `r0.30–0.35 × 0.25` on `+Z`, shaft `r0.08 × 1.2` isolated in a **`rotor` group** so it spins about Z; vent holes + side notches + plastic end-bell with bent copper tabs. |
| **Alligator leads** | `CatmullRomCurve3` with `sin(t·π)` sag → `TubeGeometry`; clip frame = wire entry at origin, mouth `+Z`; jaw is an **`ExtrudeGeometry`** with a bevel (stamped metal look), mirrored on Y with `DoubleSide` to keep winding valid, half-pitch tooth offset, chrome pivot rivet + torsion coil/legs. Clips are oriented via `setFromUnitVectors(+Z, tangent)`. |
| **Toggle switch** | Plate is split: left `PlaneGeometry` "OFF" decal on matte `#0b1220`, right **raised red `RoundedBox` with white "ON"**; lathe-rippled chrome collar + 6-gon locking nut + emissive `TorusGeometry` LED ring; lever pivots about **Z** at `y = 1.78` between `+28°` (OFF) and `−28°` (ON) with `MathUtils.damp` smoothing in `update(dt)`. |
| **Multimeter** | Holster is a `RoundedBoxGeometry` **vertex-tapered** for the ergonomic silhouette, with darker grip grooves; LCD uses a canvas texture as both `map` and `emissiveMap`; dial has 32 knurls, a chrome pointer and 5 angular range labels; 4 jacks each get ring + bore + accent + label; probes use `coiledLead()` (helix-along-axis tube) into the red/black jacks. |

All builders return a `THREE.Group` with a `.name` and a `userData` API (`setLit`, `setRPM`, `setToggle`, `setReading`, `update(dt)`) so they can be driven from your render loop without digging into the hierarchy.
